  "body": "## Summary\r\n\r\nRelates to #16.\r\n\r\nImplements Experiment 08B under `experiments/08-aks-store-demo/02-compose-to-aspire/` only:\r\n\r\n- pins .NET SDK `10.0.110` in `global.json` and Aspire AppHost SDK `13.4.6` in the AppHost project;\r\n- adds an all-container Aspire AppHost for the nine required AKS Store Demo core services;\r\n- builds application containers from the immutable Experiment 08A Dockerfiles/source snapshot;\r\n- keeps `store-front` and `store-admin` loopback-only on ports `8080` and `8081`;\r\n- keeps backend services, RabbitMQ, and DocumentDB internal;\r\n- leaves optional `ai-service` disabled by default and excluded from PASS criteria;\r\n- adds native positive, negative/recovery, cleanup, and Compose-isolation validation scripts;\r\n- records focused resource mapping, runtime contract, persistence, validation, migration assessment, and developer evidence docs.\r\n\r\n## Developer validation\r\n\r\n- `dotnet build experiments/08-aks-store-demo/02-compose-to-aspire/src/AppHost/AksStore.AppHost.csproj` PASS.\r\n- `experiments/08-aks-store-demo/02-compose-to-aspire/scripts/validate-aspire.sh --start-apphost` PASS.\r\n- `experiments/08-aks-store-demo/02-compose-to-aspire/scripts/validate-negative.sh` PASS.\r\n- Compose-only isolation check PASS: with only the Experiment 08A Compose stack running, `validate-aspire.sh --identity-only --skip-cleanup` returned non-zero with missing Aspire/DCP resource identity.\r\n- Cleanup PASS: no Experiment 08B Aspire/Compose-isolation containers remained and ports `8080`, `8081`, and `18888` were clear.\r\n- Secret scan PASS with only accepted demo credentials/placeholders detected.\r\n\r\n## Boundaries\r\n\r\nExperiment 08A, application source, cloud resources, infrastructure, active skills, and workflow configuration were not modified.\r\n\r\nThis PR is draft and should stop for human review before tester dispatch.",
